From 193c039d77232d7da8804ce8b7c0786d0a25e937 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CharlyRien <9572419+CharlyRien@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 09:13:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] Lab: XCL_FENCE_DIRECT=2 - XCL's fence probes land
 finished copies back, without a spin or a wait

With XCL_FENCE_DIRECT=1 XCL's own fence probes (alloc_pool
note_resubmits / in_flight / allocator_in_flight, sparse
drain_quarantined, list_x internal waits, vram) skipped the title
hook, and with it the hook's settle of copies back. ~480 of the ~490
GetCompletedValue calls a frame were those probes, note_resubmits once
per chunk inside every title submit: they were what put the GPU's
copies into title memory in the CPU's view before the next submit's
look and texture uploads. Without them only the readback thread (one
try_lock every 500 us, refused while the state is busy) and the
title's own ~10 fence calls a frame landed them. FIX2 (v1 + the filter
index) showed isolated green texels; FIX3 (the same without v1) none.

XCL_FENCE_DIRECT=2 keeps v1's direct read and then calls
sparse::land_finished_nowait: with copies back pending, one try_lock
of the sparse state and drain_readbacks(Drain::Finished). No spin, no
wait: a copy still running is left to the next probe, the title's
fence calls or the readback thread (the hook waited for one whose
title work was done). Unset and =1 behave as before.

Test: an adopted fence's probe, after a GPU copy into title memory and
its copy back finished, finds the bytes in the CPU's view with the
switch unset (the hook) and with v2; v1 printed only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
